---
import MarolaDoc from '../../../layouts/MarolaDoc.astro';
---

<MarolaDoc
  title="Marola — Payout setup complete"
  description="Stripe has your details. Head back to Marola to start accepting bookings."
  heading="You're set up for payouts"
>
  <p class="doc-lead">
    Stripe has what it needs. Head back to Marola, and your listings can start
    taking bookings.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="marola://connect/return" class="app-button" id="open-app">Open Marola</a>
  </p>

  <h2>If the app didn't open</h2>
  <p>
    Switch to Marola yourself and go to <strong>Profile → Payments &amp; payouts</strong>.
    It checks with Stripe each time you open it, so your status will be up to date.
  </p>
  <p>
    Stripe sometimes takes a few minutes to finish verifying, and may come back
    asking for one more detail. If it does, tap <strong>Continue payout setup</strong>
    in the app.
  </p>

  <p class="doc-note">
    Questions about payouts? Email
    <a href="mailto:hey@davidferreira.dev?subject=Marola%20payouts">hey@davidferreira.dev</a>,
    or read how fees and payouts work in the <a href="/marola/terms/">Terms</a>.
  </p>
</MarolaDoc>

<script>
  // Try the app straight away; the button stays for when that's blocked.
  window.setTimeout(() => { window.location.href = 'marola://connect/return'; }, 400);
</script>

<style>
.app-button {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  background: var(--accent);
  color: #07171E !important;
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  padding: 0.75rem 1.75rem;
  border-radius: 100px;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  transition: background 0.15s;
}
.app-button:hover { background: #e2fb8c; }
</style>
